{"repositoryId":1261573694,"availability":"available","full":"abdulla2951/PhishScope","name":"PhishScope","description":"A free, offline-first tool that analyzes URLs across 8 dimensions to detect phishing and deliver a clear risk score from 0 to 100.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-06T21:52:12Z","updated":"2026-10-14T07:31:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://abdulla2951.github.io","topics":["cli","cybersecurity","email-security","incident-response","machine-learning","phishing","phishing-detection","pytest","python","security-automation","soc-analyst","streamlit","threat-analysis"],"demo":"https://abdulla2951.github.io/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:55.478Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:55.478Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:55.478Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T02:59:55.478Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["PhishScope is a defensive-only tool. It analyzes the URLs you paste and reports phishing indicators. No offensive features, no automation of attacks against third parties."],"features":["Paste any link and get instant results. PhishScope breaks down every part of the URL to find hidden tricks.","New domains are more likely to be used for phishing. PhishScope checks when a domain was created and if it has been reported before.","A single number tells you everything. Green scores (0-30) are safe, yellow (31-60) need caution, and red (61-100) are dangerous.","Your analysis stays on your computer. No data is sent to external servers unless you choose to update threat lists.","Designed for everyday users. No confusing menus or technical terms."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/abdulla2951/PhishScope/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"91b18710104eccb165dccae9f28dbbbb67c866e1e170e7ef27d5e77d5048e827","extractedAt":"2026-10-17T02:59:55.604Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T02:5